WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.884 --> 00:00:20.968
the threat of danger from Professor Moriarty, Holmes remained cheerful as we hiked through Switzerland.

2
00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:26.331
He kept repeating that if he could rid the world of Moriarty, then he would cheerfully bring his

3
00:00:26.411 --> 00:00:28.072
career as a detective to an end.

4
00:00:28.953 --> 00:00:33.096
In one village we stayed overnight at a small hotel run by a man named Peter Steiler.

5
00:00:34.028 --> 00:00:37.610
The next day we planned to hike across the hills and spend the night in another village.

6
00:00:38.511 --> 00:00:42.514
Before we set out, Steiler told us to be sure to see the Reichenbach Falls.

7
00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:48.017
“You’ll have to make a small detour off the hiking trail,” he said, “but the view is well

8
00:00:48.037 --> 00:00:49.078
worth the extra effort.”

9
00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:51.160
We thanked him and went on our way.

10
00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:55.402
As Steiler had promised, the scenery at the falls was spectacular.

11
00:00:57.124 --> 00:00:58.144
It was also frightening.

12
00:00:59.165 --> 00:01:03.408
Swollen by melting snow, a river plunged into a deep chasm lined with black rocks.

13
00:01:04.256 --> 00:01:05.938
“Let’s walk along the path for a better view.”

14
00:01:06.978 --> 00:01:08.059
Holmes pointed ahead of us.

15
00:01:08.079 --> 00:01:10.281
“It seems to go around the falls.”

16
00:01:11.382 --> 00:01:15.886
On one side a cliff towered above us, while the falls churned and boomed below us on the

17
00:01:15.906 --> 00:01:16.406
other side.

18
00:01:16.426 --> 00:01:19.829
“Be careful, the path is very narrow,” I said.

19
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:24.313
We had stopped about halfway around the falls when Holmes spotted a boy running toward us.

20
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:30.478
“He seems in a hurry,” Holmes said, “and if I’m not mistaken, he’s carrying a message for one

21
00:01:30.518 --> 00:01:30.758
of us.”

22
00:01:31.579 --> 00:01:32.600
The boy soon reached us.

23
00:01:33.336 --> 00:01:33.876
“For Dr.

24
00:01:33.896 --> 00:01:36.857
Watson,” he said, holding out a sheet of paper.

25
00:01:38.078 --> 00:01:41.880
I took the note, which was from Steiler and written on his hotel stationery.

26
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:46.722
“Steiler says that an Englishwoman arrived at his hotel soon after we left.

27
00:01:47.842 --> 00:01:52.924
She’s very ill and bleeding heavily and—oh, dear—she has only a few hours to live.”

28
00:01:53.744 --> 00:01:56.766
I looked up at Holmes with concern and then continued reading.

29
00:01:56.786 --> 00:02:00.487
“I’m sure it would be a great comfort for her to see you,” Holmes said.

30
00:02:00.507 --> 00:02:02.168
“You must go to her at once.”

31
00:02:03.052 --> 00:02:06.013
“Yes, it’s difficult to refuse anyone dying so far from home.

32
00:02:07.013 --> 00:02:09.374
But I hesitate to leave you alone in this remote spot.”

33
00:02:10.214 --> 00:02:12.595
Holmes waved away my concern with his walking stick.

34
00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:14.215
“Don’t worry about me.

35
00:02:15.075 --> 00:02:19.076
I’m sure that, for the right price, this Swiss lad will be glad to stay as my guide

36
00:02:19.116 --> 00:02:19.736
and companion.”

37
00:02:21.417 --> 00:02:22.477
The boy nodded eagerly.

38
00:02:22.497 --> 00:02:26.898
“Well, if you’re sure I was still reluctant to leave him.

39
00:02:26.918 --> 00:02:31.820
“Go! I’ll stay here at the falls for a while and then walk slowly over the hills to

40
00:02:31.860 --> 00:02:32.620
the next village.

41
00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:34.701
You can join me there later today.”

42
00:02:35.641 --> 00:02:39.563
When I finally left my dear friend, he was leaning against a large rock and staring into the

43
00:02:39.603 --> 00:02:44.766
falls. Little did I know that this was the last time I would ever see Sherlock Holmes.

44
00:02:45.806 --> 00:02:47.147
A few minutes later, I looked back.

45
00:02:47.947 --> 00:02:51.649
I could no longer see the falls, but I could see a man hurrying toward them.

46
00:02:52.449 --> 00:02:56.811
I remember wondering where the man had come from, but my thoughts quickly turned back to the ill

47
00:02:56.851 --> 00:02:57.692
woman waiting for me.

48
00:02:59.604 --> 00:03:03.446
It took me about an hour to reach our hotel, where I found Steiler standing on the porch.

49
00:03:03.466 --> 00:03:05.086
“How is she doing?”

50
00:03:05.426 --> 00:03:05.907
I asked him.

51
00:03:05.927 --> 00:03:07.827
“Who are you talking about?”

52
00:03:08.728 --> 00:03:09.448
He looked puzzled.

53
00:03:10.308 --> 00:03:13.029
With a trembling hand, I pulled the note from my pocket.

54
00:03:13.870 --> 00:03:14.570
“Did you write this?

55
00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:17.171
Is there a sick Englishwoman here?”

56
00:03:17.191 --> 00:03:18.792
“Certainly not!”

57
00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.013
Steiler peered at the note.

58
00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:24.914
“That is our hotel stationery, but I didn’t write to you.

59
00:03:25.714 --> 00:03:28.416
It must have been written by that tall Englishman who arrived after you left.

60
00:03:28.756 --> 00:03:32.201
He said—” I didn’t wait to hear his explanation.

61
00:03:32.981 --> 00:03:36.863
I was already running down the street, heading for the hiking trail that I had just descended.

62
00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:41.145
When I finally reached the falls again, I knew my fears were justified.

63
00:03:42.986 --> 00:03:45.907
Holmes’ walking stick was leaning against the rock where I’d left him.

64
00:03:46.887 --> 00:03:49.008
But there was no other sign of him or the boy.

65
00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:52.289
“Holmes!” I shouted in every direction.

66
00:03:52.309 --> 00:03:54.470
“Holmes! Where are you?”

67
00:03:55.431 --> 00:03:56.411
There was no response.

68
00:03:57.552 --> 00:04:00.562
My heart was pounding, but I had to get control of my emotions.

69
00:04:01.563 --> 00:04:02.523
“What would Holmes do?”

70
00:04:02.924 --> 00:04:05.826
I asked myself and then realized that the answer was obvious.

71
00:04:05.846 --> 00:04:08.909
“He’d look for clues and try to figure out what happened.”

72
00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.872
Alas, it was only too easy to do.

73
00:04:12.792 --> 00:04:15.635
Holmes and I had stopped at the large rock, halfway around the falls.

74
00:04:16.616 --> 00:04:19.838
The path was soft, so it was easy for me to see many footprints.

75
00:04:20.939 --> 00:04:25.884
Beyond the rock, however, there were only two sets of footprints leading away from me, and none returning.

76
00:04:27.804 --> 00:04:31.225
A few yards from the end of the path, the grass and weeds along the edge had been

77
00:04:31.265 --> 00:04:33.306
disturbed—sure signs of a struggle.

78
00:04:34.307 --> 00:04:36.748
I lay on my stomach and peered into the chasm below.

79
00:04:36.768 --> 00:04:39.969
“Holmes!” I called again and again.

80
00:04:41.229 --> 00:04:43.250
But I heard only the echo of my own voice.

81
00:04:44.211 --> 00:04:48.192
I got up and walked back to where Holmes’ walking stick was propped against the large rock.

82
00:04:49.513 --> 00:04:52.974
Looking down, I saw something white sticking out from beneath a stone.

83
00:04:53.815 --> 00:04:57.136
I bent over and found a piece of paper torn from Holmes’ notebook.

84
00:04:58.024 --> 00:05:03.406
My dear Watson, If I may make a full confession I was convinced that the message from the

85
00:05:03.446 --> 00:05:04.347
hotel was a hoax.

86
00:05:05.467 --> 00:05:10.029
But I allowed you to leave because I thought that Professor Moriarty might appear, and indeed he has

87
00:05:10.069 --> 00:05:16.051
arrived. He has kindly permitted me to write these lines, after which we will have a final discussion

88
00:05:16.211 --> 00:05:17.832
of those issues that lie between us.

89
00:05:18.913 --> 00:05:22.874
He has already given me a description of how he avoided the police and kept himself informed of

90
00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:23.454
our movements.

91
00:05:24.515 --> 00:05:26.956
It certainly confirms my high opinion of his abilities.

92
00:05:27.968 --> 00:05:31.871
I’m happy that I will be able to free society from him, but I fear my actions will

93
00:05:31.912 --> 00:05:34.033
cause pain to my friends and especially to you.

94
00:05:35.114 --> 00:05:36.916
Do not be unduly distressed, my dear fellow.

95
00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:42.000
Tell Inspector Lestrade that the papers he needs to convict the gang are in my desk in a

96
00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.942
blue envelope marked Moriarty.

97
00:05:44.923 --> 00:05:48.365
Before leaving England I made my will and handed it to my brother, Mycroft.

98
00:05:49.366 --> 00:05:51.989
Please accept my best wishes and extend them to Mrs.

99
00:05:52.049 --> 00:05:59.841
Watson. Sincerely yours, Sherlock Holmes There is not much more for me to say about this tragedy.

100
00:06:00.781 --> 00:06:05.622
Although the local experts could not determine exactly what had happened, there was little doubt that the two

101
00:06:05.682 --> 00:06:07.503
men had plunged over the falls to their deaths.

102
00:06:08.743 --> 00:06:12.824
The Swiss boy was never found, but it was assumed that he had been hired by Moriarty and

103
00:06:12.884 --> 00:06:13.464
slipped away.

104
00:06:14.625 --> 00:06:19.206
Thanks to Holmes’ evidence, most of Moriarty’s men were later convicted at trial in London.

105
00:06:20.386 --> 00:06:25.988
As for me, I returned to England, greatly shaken by the death of Sherlock Holmes, the best and

106
00:06:26.048 --> 00:06:27.468
wisest man I ever knew.
